afe  so even though you may not get sick it's  possible that other people around you  can get sick especially if we don't take  care of ourselves so congratulations  that you wash your hands keep doing more  of that but then we need to do a little  bit more all right I want to talk about  something very disturbing that we saw  over the weekend and I'll start with  this president Trump and other officials  have been urging all of us to stop  hoarding groceries and other supplies is  the corona virus spreads what in our  psyche says  that we have to go out and buy 36 rolls  of toilet paper but leave all the soap  on the shelves yeah I think it's about  keeping up with the Joneses but in a  much more skewed way if we go into the  supermarket and we see that there's a  shelf that's empty or almost empty  then the feedback we get is oh we better  pick up the last amount or go someplace  else and get as much of that as possible  so this is a situation where it's  important that we just not follow the  crowd but follow our own hearts and  follow common sense the CDC tells us the  things that are important for us to have  and if they're not there how we can  improvise it but the important thing and  I know it's easier said than done is to  not to panic because panic will bring  out the worst in a we're seeing young  people fight over bottled water I mean  guess what  I mean it's terribly arrest but we've  got a we've got a model we've got a  model for our children the proper  behavior I like what you're saying we're  all in it together in that sense we can  model it maybe if they see some of us  staying calm that yes spread that's  great let that kindness and love spread  like contagion dr. Gardere dr. Compton  Phillips on the subject of psychology of  the virus spread I appreciate both of  you thank you we're gonna take a quick  break we'll be right back

